{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the evidence manifest of the evidence-rules slice (review\n8b1165f8, head 9c15879a, request a53e1464).\n\nThe manifest rule in docs/testing.md lists \"every file the note cites\",\nnot every file in the directory. The head's manifest lists all 27,220\nfiles (4,756,047 bytes). The recut applies the rule as written:\n\n1. The `files` list names each file the note cites, with path, bytes\n   and sha256.\n2. Where the note cites a whole directory, such as a gate run or a\n   capture, the manifest names the directory once with its file count,\n   its byte total and the sha256 of its SHA256SUMS. That directory keeps\n   its own SHA256SUMS, and the root SHA256SUMS keeps every file.\n3. The qualification line, directory path, checkpoint commit and tree\n   and the total file count stay as the rule says.\n\nThe checker verifies each listed file and each listed directory digest,\nand the root SHA256SUMS, as before. This applies to the recut of this\nhead and to later heads. The retained directory is unchanged.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8b1165f8f6117b1e1e1612073455a77cbeaf7fa9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2356b681d86d867af91ed07d208ecccfb97cfaca, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:346de78c8ca701ae95f8258752ec725a8fe18b0b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9ab75ec58e5180becc5fa5adb413bd9ce3da0d0e","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}